comments.body:
@ASAHSTM,

I completely understand the hesitation, but there are applications where you might want to capture audio at these incredibly low rates. Low-bandwidth or long-exposure applications come to mind, but also mine where I am trying to capture incredibly low frequencies and do not want to struggle against higher frequencies. 

I am trying to create a research device to test if the New Castle Method for blood pressure works. To do this, we are comparing against a the other ways to do blood pressure sampling (auscultatory and oscillometric). This is specficially for the auscultatory method, where we will be using an analog stethoscope to record the person's heartbeat to an SD card. We want to take advantage of Nyquists' Theory as much as possible so we do not have to do as much signal processing, especially since we are trying looking at sounds in the 20-120 Hz range.
